# The configure step refuses a standard library without the floating-point
# std::from_chars (#654): GCC 9.5's libstdc++ failed deep in the build, at
# lib/Driver/Gromacs.cpp. Inputs/float_from_chars.py configures a small
# project with cmake/CheckFloatFromChars.cmake twice: with the compiler of
# the machine, and with a wrapper of it that rejects <charconv>'s floating
# std::from_chars as such a library does.
# RUN: rm -rf %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/float_from_chars.py %S/../../cmake/CheckFloatFromChars.cmake %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: the compiler of the machine: configured
# CHECK-NEXT: a library without it: refused
# CHECK-NEXT: MDIR needs a C++ standard library with the floating-point std::from_chars of C++17 (std::chars_format)
# CHECK-NEXT: use GCC 11 or later, or a Clang whose libc++ or libstdc++ has it
